WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:08.860
We belong to the UEAF, but we aren't assigned to any group,

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.650
making the Nadesico an oddball unit no one wants to claim.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.110
Then we get these two fools all picky about regulations aboard.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.040
While these three are still in the midst of a romantic battle royale.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.470
These three act like real big shots.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.300
Detecting a Chulip approaching Earth!

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:00.970
Second Defensive Line

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.840
Chulip has entered our Second Defensive Line air space!

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.430
Forth Defensive Line

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.510
The Dangers of Femininity

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.150
So, we've been given the mission of investigating and collecting

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.770
this new generation Chulip that impacted on Tenician Island.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.440
And this mission was assigned to us,

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.370
because my Nadesico and I are of such superior caliber!

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.990
So, what's going on here?!

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:04.610
Why hasn't anyone come to the bridge to listen to my orders?!

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:08.000
Currently it is 2 AM in our theater of operations.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.880
In Japan, it's referred to as the third hour of the Ox.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.570
Usually people are asleep at this time of the night.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.560
What the hell?!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.960
The Nadesico is a combat vessel! This can't be right!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:18.660
Good night...

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.090
The Nadesico is a combat vessel! This can't be right!

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.470
Hey, wait a minute! You're the helmswoman!

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.380
You need to stay at your post!

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.020
But it's time for the end of my shift.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.910
Hey! You will listen to me when I address you, Haruka Minato!

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.050
All yours!

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.150
Thanks a lot!

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:28.730
Hey! You will listen to me when I address you, Haruka Minato!

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.850
Come back here! And anyway, where is the Captain?!

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:32.290
Everyone is slacking off too much!  When I was young...

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.350
On the equator...

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:33.670
Everyone is slacking off too much!  When I was young...

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.570
Tenician Island...

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.030
Everyone is slacking off too much!  When I was young...

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.070
Coral reefs and sandy beaches...

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.780
It looks like I'll have it ready.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.120
Yes! It won't do any good just waiting for something to happen.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.160
I need to do as Megumi-san does.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.410
I should make late night snacks for him like this!

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.920
I was wondering why she suddenly asked to use the kitchen.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.270
Then...

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.690
Here you are!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.320
Delicious!

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.150
I'm glad you liked it!

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:23.870
It was wonderful, Yurika. Better than anything I've tasted before.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.910
This is about all I can do for you.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.790
Yurika, I'm sorry I didn't realize sooner.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.860
Akito...

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:35.750
Oh no!

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.670
Why?! What's going on?!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.080
Tenkawa sure is one unlucky guy!

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:49.810
Depressing...

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.150
I need something to fill this void that ravages me so.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.940
That's it!

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.650
A midnight snack filled with love.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.820
A meal prepared for me?!

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.160
Good night, Jun-kun!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.450
Yurika!

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:08.830
BAKA-bakka

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.560
Get a hold of yourself!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.170
Who are you?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.790
Who... Who am I?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.760
I can't remember anything.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.030
Man, this is where it gets interesting.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:21.230
We'll get you patched up!

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:21.630
Right!

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.430
Akito, I prepared a midnight snack for you.
Can I come in?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.110
Sure.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.910
You're watching anime again?

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:31.350
Yeah...

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:36.520
This is the first time I've ever worn clothing like this.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.700
So, what's the story in this one, Akito?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.670
This doesn't fit me, does it?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:40.790
Oh no, you're wonderful. You look gorgeous in it.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.740
This is episode 33,
"The Smile of Holy Maiden Aquamarine".

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:44.450
Thank you.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.750
Aquamarine, that young girl, is an enemy pilot for the Gemini Robot.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.600
She gets amnesia, and falls in love with the main character.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.290
Oh, wait for me, Ken!
She gets amnesia, and falls in love with the main character.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:53.040
Slow poke! Come on!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.020
This guest character Aquamarine is quite a girl!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.400
She's great at cooking and...

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.540
So, you like girls who can cook?!

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.990
Akito, I made this all for you! Please have some!

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.200
Sure...

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:06.010
Come on!

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.930
Go ahead!

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.010
Come on, Akito!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:12.430
Sure...

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.530
Okay?

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.320
Akito-san!

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.040
Are you all right, Akito-san?!

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.540
Water!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.830
Akito-san!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.240
Water...

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.500
Have this stamina building juice!

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:44.400
What's going on?! It smells like poison gas in here!

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.580
Well, you see...

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.510
Megumi-san, what did you put in that?!

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.480
Dokudami, sanshou, shiitake mushrooms, burdock, lotus root,

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.320
the blood of snapping turtles and pit vipers, cow liver.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:57.230
I also mixed a few nutrition and energy drinks.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:00.770
Why you little...

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.510
Get the hell out of my room!

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.110
What did you eat?!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.540
Carry him to sickbay, immediately.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.430
And discard that pot on the double!

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:13.730
Is this some new attack that the Jovians are using?

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.040
You could call it the fatal poison of love.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:17.540
Wonderful! Delicious!

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.050
This really tastes great!

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:22.950
I always told myself,
I'd marry a girl who's a real good cook!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.340
Really?

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.500
Akito, this time I made sure it tastes good!

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.740
Akito-san, I did too!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:31.710
Akito!

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:32.950
Akito-san!

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.400
Die, Gekiganger 3!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:45.750
Akito?

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.320
Akito-san?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.200
What are you doing, Aquamarine?!

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.240
Aquamarine!

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.420
Ken...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.660
I know my time with you was brief, but I was happy.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.580
Aquamarine! No!

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.230
I love you!

00:07:58.480 --> 00:07:59.250
Farewell!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.340
Aquamarine!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:06.210
Ken!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.190
Life would be a breeze if there really were girls like her around.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.870
Lower the Nadesico near the reef!

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:18.010
Prepare the landing party!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:18.680
Yes, Sir!

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.250
Here, Ruri-ruri, you're very pale, so you'll need this UV blocker.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.560
Thank you.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.280
I've never been to the ocean.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.000
Somehow, I'm happy.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.950
Beach umbrella unit, forward!

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:38.910
Right!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.710
Don't let the women have all the glory!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:41.330
Yes, Sir!

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.750
Wait a minute, all of you!

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.430
Are you aware of what you're doing?

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:48.670
You are all employees of Nergal Heavy Industries!

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:49.880
That means...

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.770
The time you spend playing will be deducted from your pay.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.300
All right, here's a brochure I made for spending time on the beach.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.220
Make sure not to go into deeper parts of the ocean.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.140
Wear sandals on rocky surfaces.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.580
Do not use suntan lotions that are non-biodegradable.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.190
And...

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.750
Geez! Can't they even take the time to read the brochure?!

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.540
Step right up!

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.930
The most important features of the beach are the powdery curry,

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.950
ramen that tastes bad and shaved ice that's mostly melted!

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.050
I will now pass down that heritage to a new generation!

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:33.020
For this is the last of an ancient tradition: the beach tea house!

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:33.750
Ramen, please.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.760
Be right up!

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.300
Daruma's dolly's falling down

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.540
There you go!

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:45.900
Tastes horrible.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.350
You betcha!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.200
Tenkawa-kun!

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:52.650
I have a few things I want to ask you.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.360
You came from Mars, right?

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.490
Yes...

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.220
Yes, well... would you like some?

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:02.730
I'm sorry!

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:04.370
Hey, Tenkawa-kun!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.220
Geez!

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:09.790
Tastes horrible.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.590
Oh boy...

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.540
Oh! I'm sorry.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:21.390
I've found you! My prince charming!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.760
Aquamarine!

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:36.280
What on Earth is going on here?!

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:40.460
Hey, you! Do you realize that we're on a mission?!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.660
What about searching for the new Chulip? Well?!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.500
Why aren't any of you answering me?!

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.690
I've had about enough of this.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.930
Yeah, bury him! Bury him!

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.260
What do you think you're doing?! Stop that!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.140
Oh, this is part of teamwork training!

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.970
Well! Do you think you'll get away with this?!

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:06.100
I'm an admiral! An admiral...

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:14.650
Hey! Hey, you! Come here and get me out!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.670
I said come back, right now!

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:41.260
I'm Tenkawa Akito.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:41.890
And you are?

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.740
Aqua...

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.310
I'm Aqua.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.060
Aqua?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:49.980
Yes.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:56.300
I wonder where Akito went to?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.850
Akito-san!

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:08.600
A hat?

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.710
A woman's hat!

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:11.710
Whose is it?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.560
Please.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:18.430
Help yourself.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:20.050
I hope you won't mind if I do.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:23.300
This is great!

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.350
Oh, thank goodness!

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:30.270
What's the matter?

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.310
Oh no, it's nothing!

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.400
By the way...

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.230
Just call me Aqua.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.430
Aqua, do you live alone here?

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:40.190
Where are your parents?

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.450
Both my father and mother died.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.630
I'm an orphan all alone in this world.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.200
All alone...

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:49.990
I'm sorry.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.160
Oh no, it's all right.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:52.620
After all...

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.800
All right, everyone. Time to start the search.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.610
Yeah, sure.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.070
Hey!

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:12.620
What about me?! Where do you think you're going?!

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:17.070
Where's the Captain?

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.450
Has she drowned?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.740
Come to think about it, Akito and Megumi-san are missing as well.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.140
Wait a minute!

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.490
There's nothing to worry about with those three together!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:33.110
It looks like this island passed into private ownership recently.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:36.670
It's part of the Crimson Estate the largest Australian conglomerate.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.090
The Crimsons?

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.790
I know them!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:43.680
They just made the news recently when their only daughter debuted.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.250
Crimson...

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.720
They're one of the top makers of energy barrier systems.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.790
They made the barrier satellites above us as well.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:56.280
But I recall their lone daughter is a real problem child.

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.020
Problem child?

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.940
Adding a paralyzing drug to dinner party's entrees without reason.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.860
Kidnapping a manga author so she could have her own girl's comic.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:10.350
It's the one stain on the otherwise perfect profile of the Crimsons.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:15.160
That must be the new Chulip.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.500
Guess it's time to destroy it.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:18.500
Wait just a second!

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:22.960
A barrier?

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.460
The Crimson's emblem?

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.890
A barrier? What's going on here?

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.390
It's no concern of ours. Let's blow it all up.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.680
What's going on here? Why have the Crimsons erected a barrier?

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:44.490
Ever since my mother and father died,
I've been all alone.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.440
Aqua...

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:48.960
But then I was able to meet you.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.370
You're the knight in shining armor that I've longed to meet!

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.520
I feel the same. You mean so much to me!

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:02.210
Akito, I don't ever want to leave your side.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:05.390
Aqua...

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.680
Please, stay with me forever.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.110
Akito!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:12.140
Akito-san!

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:16.680
Who are they?

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:17.680
Oh,

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.050
nice to meet you!

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.510
That's not important!

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.320
Who is this person?!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.980
Well, you see...

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.240
It seems we're at an end.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.410
The barrier is down!

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:39.750
What the hell?

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.330
Oh God, it's a huge Jiro!

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:50.420
It looks like this new Chulip isn't an exit gate for boson jumping.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.350
Instead it's a large transport vessel.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.490
The enemy might be trying different tactics.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.270
It looks like it isn't fully operational.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.270
Neutralize it, please.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.290
Akito, who is that girl?!

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.660
Hey you, get away from Akito-san right now!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:13.490
Wait a minute, she's...

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:15.030
She's...

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:17.910
She's like Aquamarine to me!

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.410
Are you all right, Aqua?

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:29.510
I'm so happy!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.260
We're about to meet our doom!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.370
My dream will finally come true.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:48.230
Lovers that perish in the flames of battle!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.190
Oh, it's so romantic!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.990
What are you saying, Aqua? ....

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.030
I've been waiting for this! This very moment!

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.960
The couple deep in love, dying in beauty.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:02.710
Yes, I will be the perfect tragic heroine!

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:08.290
Akito, get away from that girl! Something isn't right about her!

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.760
You, let go of Akito-san!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:19.980
It looks like the paralysis drug is starting to kick in.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.190
Akito!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.550
Why are you doing such a horrible thing?!

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.830
If you want to die, why don't you go ahead and do it alone?

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.140
You'll never understand!

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.500
I grew up as a child with all that I wanted within my reach.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.420
I longed for this! To be a tragic heroine!

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:49.960
Tragic?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:50.630
Heroine?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.800
Being too happy was my unhappiness.

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:58.180
I'll perish together with my lover in the flames of war!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.930
That Chulip was a gift from God to me!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.850
No! Get me out of here!

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:09.270
Akito, we'll never be separated. We'll ascend into beauty today!

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:10.680
Akito!

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:11.780
Akito-san!

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.440
No!

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.850
Akito!

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:24.040
Akito-san!

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:30.580
Damn you!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:37.970
Are you all right, Akito?!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.170
Akito! What the hell are you doing?!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.890
Ryoko, behind you!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:46.720
Shut up!

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.610
Yeah, do it! Knock him dead!

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:52.850
Beat the living daylights out of him, please!

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:02.870
Scary...

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.000
Akito, come back!

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:24.970
Let us together play the parts of a great tragedy!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.640
You ate that girl's cooking, right?

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:34.860
Won't you eat mine then?

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.200
No, that's not what I had in mind.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.840
Akito!

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:43.170
I tried to do some cooking as well.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.410
Someone help me!

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:49.330
Akito!

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.460
Akito-san!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.250
Please, eat my cooking!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.470
You have to leave me alone!

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:01.680
I'm the tragic protagonist!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.300
Liar...

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.210
Happiness for one person is misery for another.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.690
There's nothing sweeter than the unhappiness of others.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.090
I envy him so.

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:17.790
Hey!

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:18.970
Wait!

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:21.270
What about me?!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:26.120
Soon the tide will come in, and both of us will be underwater.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.310
Why are you giggling? What's with this girl!

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.040
Somebody help me!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:32.870
Let's obtain happiness!
Somebody help me!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.080
Let's obtain happiness!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.630
I'm definitely not happy!

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.240
Will it be like the movie "The Battle of the Bulge", "Patton",

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.670
"The Liberation of Europe", "The Beast"

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:51.710
or " An Idiot Comes On A Tank"?

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:52.830
Tanks!

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.170
Artifacts of a bygone era come alive to the sound of metal treads.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:59.510
Old friendships are rekindled and the flames of passion burn bright!

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:02.320
Hiroyuki "X" Kawasaki of "Irresponsible Captain Tyler" fame

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.720
will make all of you witnesses to the tears of time!

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.410
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:08.550
"Finding Yourself in a Routine Plot"

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:11.440
Let's watch it, everyone!
